==English==
[[Image:BlurryDavid.jpg|thumb|right|A blurry photo.]]

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|blur|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈblɜːɹi/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-blurry.wav |Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜːɹi|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|of an image}} Not [[clear]], [[crisp]], or [[focus]]ed; having [[fuzzy]] edges.
#: {{ux|en|If I take off my glasses, everything close up looks '''blurry'''.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Not [[clear]]; lacking well-defined boundaries.
#: {{ux|en|It would seem that the line between flirting and sexual harassment has become quite '''blurry'''.}}
#*{{quote-journal|en
|date=October 15 2020
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/news/2020/oct/15/dangerous-rise-of-military-ai-drone-swarm-autonomous-weapons
|work=The Guardian
|author=Frank Pasquale
|title=‘Machines set loose to slaughter’: the dangerous rise of military AI
|passage= when it comes to the future of war, the line between science fiction and industrial fact is often '''blurry'''.}}

